From 2186548d5af38b6ab06379a38b9f8fc7a08636bc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: vince <vincepaul.liem@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:52:26 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(launch): preserve virtual root ownership on assigned
 storage

Handle chown variants through existing inode, path and descriptor owners.
Accept root or unchanged IDs on existing storage objects without issuing host
ownership calls, including no-follow and empty-path descriptor operations.

Signed-off-by: vince <vincepaul.liem@gmail.com>
---
 README.md                               |  5 +++
 crates/ginux-init/src/descriptors.rs    |  7 +++-
 crates/ginux-init/src/fs_hooks.rs       | 53 +++++++++++++++++++++++--
 scripts/test-launch-storage.py          |  3 +-
 tests/fixtures/launch-storage-fixture.c | 27 +++++++++++++
 5 files changed, 88 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 92f9a305..565f58a9 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -445,3 +445,8 @@ checks for syscall ABI dispatch, clone restrictions, descriptor inheritance,
 thread reuse, successful and failed worker exec, signals, wait-status writes,
 nonblocking waits, and vfork. The existing native fork fixture also runs. These
 checks do not claim complete libc, job-control, or systemd compatibility.
+
+Owned storage inode uid/gid are virtual root. `chown`, `fchown`, `lchown` and
+`fchownat` can preserve 0 or unchanged (-1) on existing assigned storage objects,
+including symlinks and empty-path descriptor operations. Other identities remain
+unsupported; these operations never change host ownership.
